2 17592186045443 true] [17592186521978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521978 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the level surface $\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(y - 2\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right)=0$ at the point $(0,3,-3).$" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521978 1072 #uuid "4bb06bb9-e449-5e9a-8e4e-1903c28e4441" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521978 1074 "Let's set $f(x,y,z)=\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(y - 2\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right).$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(0,3,-3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,3,-3).$\n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,3,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)&={f}_{x}(x,y,z)i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)k\\\\&=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(y - 2\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right))i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(y - 2\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right))j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(y - 2\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right))k\\\\&=\\left(2 x + 2\\right)i+\\left(4 y - 8\\right)j+\\left(1\\right)k\\\\∇f(0,3,-3)&=\\left(2\\right)i+\\left(4\\right)j+\\left(1\\right)k\\\\&=⟨2,4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(0,3,-3)$ and passes through the point $(0,3,-3)$ can be written as\n\n$$r=⟨0,3,-3⟩+t\\,∇f(0,3,-3)=⟨0,3,-3⟩+t\\,⟨2,4,1⟩.$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521979 1080 "r=⟨0,-2,-3⟩+t\\,⟨0,-4,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521979 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521979 1083 #uuid "50a7485f-6811-5e77-b09e-a7a14f6345ff" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521980 1080 "r=⟨1,2,-3⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521980 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521980 1083 #uuid "5768953d-f1c1-5d2c-893e-6ad0d8c70929" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521981 1080 "r=⟨0,3,-3⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521981 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521981 1083 #uuid "58e583f7-1a74-515f-a245-2588bfab496b" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521982 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521971 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521982 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521982 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the level surface $\\left(-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(z - 2\\right)=0$ at the point $(0,-3,5).$" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521982 1072 #uuid "6dd1fd09-3ea2-5abd-b9f4-b090d278c7fb" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521982 1074 "Let's set $f(x,y,z)=\\left(-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(z - 2\\right).$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(0,-3,5)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,-3,5).$\n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,-3,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)&={f}_{x}(x,y,z)i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)k\\\\&=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\left(-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(z - 2\\right))i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\left(-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(z - 2\\right))j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\left(-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(z - 2\\right))k\\\\&=\\left(2 x - 2\\right)i+\\left(4 y + 8\\right)j+\\left(-1\\right)k\\\\∇f(0,-3,5)&=\\left(-2\\right)i+\\left(-4\\right)j+\\left(-1\\right)k\\\\&=⟨-2,-4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(0,-3,5)$ and passes through the point $(0,-3,5)$ can be written as\n\n$$r=⟨0,-3,5⟩+t\\,∇f(0,-3,5)=⟨0,-3,5⟩+t\\,⟨-2,-4,-1⟩.$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521983 1080 "r=⟨0,1,1⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521983 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521983 1083 #uuid "76b8c1ca-8da8-54f0-8d8a-39244f16536c" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521984 1080 "r=⟨2,2,-3⟩+t\\,⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521984 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521984 1083 #uuid "81784560-888a-501c-bd67-ea96c214e504" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521985 1080 "r=⟨0,-3,5⟩+t\\,⟨-2,0,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521985 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521985 1083 #uuid "84b579e9-9396-5375-a1aa-9e672056b65e" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521986 1080 "r=⟨0,-3,5⟩+t\\,⟨0,-4,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521986 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521986 1083 #uuid "8ba36e9d-1dd3-5777-8a5b-96b89bca0937" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521987 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521991 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521987 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521987 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the level surface $\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+2\\left(-\\left(y + 1\\right)\\right)^{2}-\\left(-z\\right)=0$ at the point $(0,-2,-3).$" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521987 1072 #uuid "8bfc56db-f764-5bb9-b626-8a45b50e648a" 13194139535602 17592186045443 true] [17592186521987 1074 "Let's set $f(x,y,z)=\\left(x + 1\\rig